;; spec:   stdlib §8.1 item 2 (the model test of Map), types §2.13
;; expect: accept
;; result: 0
;; audit:  clean
;; roots:  support
;; The prelude's Map is a hash array mapped trie: a leaf per key, a bucket for
;; keys whose hashes are equal, a bitmap node five bits of the hash at a time.
;; Here the key is the i64 itself, which hashes to itself: ids 0 to 31 each
;; take a slot of the root, ids 32 to 59 share a slot with 0 to 27 and go one
;; level down. It is the map of a program as it is usually written.
;; 14 seeded sequences (seeds 853000 to 853013) of 72 operations over 60 keys
;; run on a Map and on a model, an array indexed by key id (tl.model says why
;; it is not the page's association Vec). An operation is a put of a random
;; value or a delete, the share of puts falling from 85 to 50 to 4 in a hundred
;; over a sequence, so the map fills, mixes and drains; a put is aimed at a key
;; the map has not got every other time and a delete at one it has five times
;; in six, so the map grows, overwrites, drains and, now and then, deletes what
;; is not there. After every operation the counts agree, `get` and `contains?`
;; of each of the 60 keys agree, and a full `for-each` visits the model's keys
;; once each with the model's values; a snapshot every sixth operation is
;; checked again at the end, against its own model, after every map built on
;; it. The totals the sequences reached (puts of a key already there, deletes
;; of a key that was there, deletes of one that was not, times the map went
;; from some entries to none, the most entries it held) are asserted too, so a
;; generator that stopped reaching an edge fails the case. The faults planted
;; are in the model (tl.model): one that keeps a key's old value when it is put
;; again, one that deletes the wrong key; each must make some sequence of four
;; fail.
(ns main (:use tl.check tl.model))

;; n sequences, one check each: bit i of the result is the sequence of seed base + i
(defun run-many (c: Checks cv: Cover base: i64 n: i64 fault: i64) -> unit
  (dotimes (i n) (check c (= 0 (run-map-seq (+ base i) 60 72 mk-int id-int fault cv)))))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((c (checks))
        (p1 (checks))
        (p2 (checks))
        (cv (cover)))
    (do (run-many c cv 853000 14 0)
        (run-many p1 (cover) 853000 4 1)
        (run-many p2 (cover) 853000 4 2)
        (check c (>= @(. cv overwrites) 30))
        (check c (>= @(. cv deletes) 200))
        (check c (>= @(. cv absent) 80))
        (check c (>= @(. cv emptied) 10))
        (check c (>= @(. cv peak) 18))
        (check-detects c p1)
        (check-detects c p2)
        (checks-result c))))
